    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94503.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Well, yes, good morning. Thank you for inviting me to join you. It is always an honor to be with you. You know, I think one of the greatest challenges that our country has had is that China has been purposefully passing their own law and taking certain positions and starting certain off that target American interests and do things that American citizens and certainly leaders may not even realizing are working in the interest to strengthen China and their military development and their economic strength over our own. And one of the things that we uncovered was that, you know, leading up into the Biden administration, they had actually passed the law. that said their national, so Chinese nationals, had to cooperate with matters regarding their own national security and that they had to cooperate with intelligence gathering or face consequences. So think about that. If you're a Chinese national, there's now a law that you have to assist the CCP in intelligence gathering by law or face consequences. So why in the world? would America have not cut off the ability for Chinese nationals to come and be students here if they are going to be enlisted in intelligence gathering. It's right there in their log.",
