  {
    "episode_id": 94503,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94503.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "But simply, there are so many of these instances, whether they're setting up police stations within our country, whether it's feeling intellectual property from our university, whether it's passing these laws and sending students here. It is incredible the amount of, I would say, ops that they have been able to develop that are subversive to the strengths of our nation. And we just have to make sure that we are staying on top of this. And as they are adjusting their laws and their programs that are seeking to intelligence gather from our nation, that we are reacting. And you know, it's great to see a president that has come into office and said, enough is enough. Like, what have we been doing? I mean, are we asleep at the wheel? I'm a brand new senator. My whole job before as Attorney General was to protect the interests and security and rights of my citizens. and the state of Florida. I bring that same deal here on behalf not just of my state, but America. And I am loving that I get to start my tenure as a United States Senator. I've been in office two months now. With a president that says this cannot happen anymore, we cannot allow other nation states to eat our lunch while we're asleep at the wheel. We have got to be putting our country first. And that doesn't mean we don't want to work with others to foster peace and to foster security and to make sure that the world is a safe place. But we have to start paying attention to America's interests and putting our country and our citizens first, and I just appreciate so much working with a commander-in-chief who does just that.",
